            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Some of the data collected here appears to overlap with information already gathered by existing dreport plugins. For example:\n\nps -l provides information similar to what is available from the existing top -n 1 -b plugin\nfree -h overlaps conceptually with the data collected by the meminfo plugin\n\nThis overlap does not seem problematic, but it may be worth considering whether these commands add distinct value beyond what is already available. Otherwise, these could potentially be trimmed to reduce redundancy."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ninad Palsule",
                        "email": "ninad@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "ninadpalsule"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, Removed \"free -h\" but need to keep \"ps -l\" as top command doesn't print RSS ```Mem: 304600K used, 521444K free, 1000K shrd, 16840K buff, 146516K cached\nCPU:   4% usr   9% sys   0% nic   0% idle  86% io   0% irq   0% sirq\nLoad average: 0.83 0.63 0.58 1/218 2948\n  PID  PPID USER     STAT   VSZ %VSZ CPU %CPU COMMAND\n 1070     1 root     S    58368   7%   1   9% /usr/bin/vpd-manager\n 2948  2811 root     R     2852   0%   0   5% top -n 1 -b\n 1058     1 root     S    71556   9%   0   0% mboxd --flash 64M --window-size 1M --window-num 63\n 1029     1 root     S    69064   8%   0   0% /usr/bin/mctp-demux-daemon astlpc /dev/raw-kcs3\n  380     1 root     S    29180   4%   1   0% /usr/lib/systemd/systemd-journald\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/dreport.d/plugins.d/perfdata",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "NIT: Two separate command invocations Slightly more overhead chnage to  add_cmd_output \"echo -e '\\n[ps -l]'; ps -l\" \"$file_name\" \"ps long\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/dreport.d/plugins.d/perfdata",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ninad Palsule",
                        "email": "ninad@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "ninadpalsule"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, make sense. done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/dreport.d/plugins.d/perfdata",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
